    "op": "UPDATE",
    "entry_id": "945ef3e8",
    "content": "* * MANDATORY scope definition workflow (export/backup/collection tasks) — execute BEFORE collecting ANY data: (1) List ALL available data endpoints for the platform. (2) Print a SCOPE TABLE: for each endpoint, write IN-SCOPE or OUT-OF-SCOPE. DEFAULT IS OUT-OF-SCOPE — to promote to IN-SCOPE, you MUST paste a DIRECT QUOTE from the task instruction that explicitly requests this data source. Paraphrasing or self-invented justifications are NOT valid. 'Song library' → show_song_library ONLY; 'library' alone → primary library for the entity mentioned; 'all data' → everything. Albums, playlists, liked/followed content are SEPARATE collections — each requires its OWN justifying quote from the task. If you cannot find a quote, the endpoint stays OUT. (3) Collect ONLY from in-scope endpoints. PROGRESSIVE SIZE GATE: After adding each new source, compare total unique items to the primary source count. If total exceeds 2× the primary source, STOP immediately — you are almost certainly over-expanding scope. (4) Print final item count and scope justification (with task quotes) before writing any output file."
